The installed app: PWA manifest and the workbench's install metadata.

code-server's generated manifest is code-server's: it asks for fullscreen
display, offers window-controls-overlay, and describes itself as "Run Code on
a remote server." The workbench's apple-mobile-web-app-title - the name iOS
writes under a home-screen icon, which takes precedence over the manifest's
short_name - is still "Code".

Colours are the brand backgrounds, the same pair the first-paint block in
these files already uses. A "PWA install metadata" test in
tests/code-server-patches.test.ts pins them to packages/shared.

diff --git a/src/node/routes/vscode.ts b/src/node/routes/vscode.ts
--- a/src/node/routes/vscode.ts
+++ b/src/node/routes/vscode.ts
@@ -182,9 +182,19 @@
           name: req.args["app-name"],
           short_name: req.args["app-name"],
           start_url: ".",
-          display: "fullscreen",
-          display_override: ["window-controls-overlay"],
-          description: "Run Code on a remote server.",
+          // standalone, not fullscreen: an installed editor keeps the clock and
+          // battery visible like every other app. display_override is dropped
+          // with it - window-controls-overlay would let the OS controls sit on
+          // top of our own titlebar, which does not reserve titlebar-area-*.
+          display: "standalone",
+          description:
+            "Composery is an always-on cloud IDE: VS Code in the browser or on your phone, self-hosted on your own server or managed in Composery Cloud, and made for long-running AI agents.",
+          // Brand dark background, matching the maskable launcher icon's tile, so
+          // the Android splash and status bar are continuous with the icon the
+          // user just tapped. A manifest carries one value; the workbench's
+          // theme-color meta corrects the status bar per scheme once it paints.
+          theme_color: "#0a0a0a",
+          background_color: "#0a0a0a",
           icons: [192, 512]
             .map((size) => [
               {
